  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - TULCEA WATER AND WASTEWATER SYSTEM IMPROVEMENTS, through Government of Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $330,400 Feasibility Study on the Tulcea Water and Wastewater System Improvements project (a) examines and proposes rehabilitation methods for neglected water distribution and sewerage systems in the developed areas of Tulcea County, Romania, and (b) examines alternatives to the use of gaseous chlorine for the potable water disinfection in Romania&apos;s easternmost city of Sulina. These improvements will improve resource efficiency, reduce costs and eliminate environmental risks associated with wastewater leakage and gaseous chlorine transport.</narrative>
  </description>
